    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 22 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Empty your hand before opponents. The team of the player who goes out first wins; the team of the player who goes out last loses. Score depends on how quickly both team members empty their hands.',
      'Turn-flow example: Cards are drawn one at a time anticlockwise; first three players get 22 cards each, last two get 21. During or after drawing, a player may expose an Ace to make it the Big Ace and become declarer; the holder of the matching Ace is the secret partner. Play: declarer or partner (if revealed) leads any single or combination. In turn each player passes or plays a higher combination of the same type. Four consecutive passes clear the pile and the last player leads again. First team to empty both hands wins; scoring is by finish order and doubles if partner revealed their Ace.',
      "Scoring example: Zero-sum scoring. Points based on the order teammates finish. If partner's Ace was revealed before play, scoring is doubled. Solo declarer wins by finishing first, loses by finishing last. Cumulative score over multiple deals..",
